@node Starting out
@section Starting out

@findex niori
@kindex C-c M
Type @kbd{M-x niori} to open the dashboard and enable the key bindings.
The command turns on @code{niori-mode}, a global minor mode, so the
@kbd{C-c M} prefix works in every buffer; until then Niori has zero
footprint in your Emacs.  Everything is reachable from the dashboard's
buttons, or from the keyboard:

@table @kbd
@item C-c M d
@kindex C-c M d
Open the dashboard (@pxref{The dashboard}).
@item C-c M m
@kindex C-c M m
Medications roster (@pxref{Medications}).
@item C-c M v
@kindex C-c M v
Visits roster (@pxref{Visits and letters}).
@item C-c M t
@kindex C-c M t
Lab tests roster (@pxref{Lab tests}).
@item C-c M c
@kindex C-c M c
Vaccinations roster (@pxref{Vaccinations}).
@item C-c M a @var{module}
@kindex C-c M a
Start a new record: @kbd{C-c M a m} for a medication, and likewise for
visits, lab tests and vaccinations (@pxref{Forms}).
@item C-c M E o
@itemx C-c M E c
@itemx C-c M E j
@kindex C-c M E
Export a module as Org, CSV or FHIR JSON (@pxref{Exporting data}).
@item C-c M D
@kindex C-c M D
Diff a record against its last revision (@pxref{History and
revisions}).
@item C-c M f
@kindex C-c M f
Show every document you have attached (@pxref{Documents}).
@item C-c M l
@kindex C-c M l
Compose a letter from a visit (@pxref{Visits and letters}).
@item C-c M b
@kindex C-c M b
Back up the database (@pxref{Backups}).
@item C-c M ?
@kindex C-c M ?
Open the transient command menu (when @code{transient} is installed).
@item C-c M C-h
@kindex C-c M C-h
Show a full overview of every Niori key binding.
@end table

@noindent
CUA bindings (@kbd{C-x}/@kbd{C-c}/@kbd{C-v} cut/copy/paste) are
available for standalone users: set @code{niori-standalone-cua} to
@code{t}, or type @kbd{M-x cua-mode} anytime.  Text size follows the
desktop zoom keys @kbd{C-=}, @kbd{C-+} and @kbd{C--} (@pxref{Text
size}).

@node The dashboard
@section The dashboard

@cindex dashboard
@findex niori-dashboard
The dashboard is Niori's home screen; @kbd{M-x niori-dashboard} also
opens it directly.  Each module contributes a section, so one buffer
shows, at a glance:

@itemize @bullet
@item
your active medications;
@item
upcoming visits, within @code{niori-visits-upcoming-days} days
(default 30);
@item
the latest result of each lab test, with abnormal results flagged;
@item
vaccinations whose booster is due or overdue, within
@code{niori-vaccinations-due-days} days (default 90).
@end itemize

@noindent
Entries are buttons: follow one to open the record's detail view.
After every write, Niori refreshes any open dashboard, roster and
detail buffers for the affected module, so what you see is always
current.

@node Rosters
@section Rosters

@cindex rosters
A roster lists all records of one kind in a sortable
@code{tabulated-list-mode} buffer.  Open one from the dashboard or with
@kbd{C-c M m} (medications), @kbd{C-c M v} (visits), @kbd{C-c M t} (lab
tests) or @kbd{C-c M c} (vaccinations).

@table @kbd
@item RET
Open the record under point in its detail view.
@item a
Add a new record (the same form as @kbd{C-c M a @dots{}}).
@item e
Edit the record under point.
@item d
Delete the record under point; Niori asks first
(@pxref{Attachment safety}).
@item g
Refresh the roster.
@item S
Sort; clicking a column header sorts as well.
@item D
Diff the record under point against its previous revision
(@pxref{History and revisions}).
@item E
Export the module (@pxref{Exporting data}).
@item L
Compose a letter from the visit under point (visits roster only,
@pxref{Visits and letters}).
@end table

@node Forms
@section Forms

@cindex forms
@cindex validation
Records are created and edited in @code{widget} forms: buffers with
labelled, validated fields, including checks on dates, so invalid data
never reaches the database.

@table @kbd
@item C-c C-c
@kindex C-c C-c
Save the record.
@item C-c C-k
@kindex C-c C-k
Cancel and leave the form.
@end table

@node Detail views
@section Detail views

@cindex detail views
The detail view describes one record read-only, with buttons for the
actions that apply to it.  It also accepts the roster keys: @kbd{e}
edits, @kbd{d} deletes, @kbd{D} diffs against the previous revision,
@kbd{L} composes a letter, and @kbd{E} opens the export menu.  In
every detail view, @kbd{A} attaches a document to the record
(@pxref{Documents}).  After a write, all open buffers of that module
refresh automatically.

@node Medications
@section Medications

@cindex medications
The medications module tracks name, dosage, form, dates, prescriber and
instructions for each medication.  The dashboard lists your active
medications.  Open the roster with @kbd{C-c M m}; start a new record
with @kbd{C-c M a m}, or with @kbd{a} from the roster.

@node Visits and letters
@section Visits and letters

@cindex visits
@cindex letters
The visits module tracks date, doctor, facility, reason, diagnosis and
notes for each visit; the dashboard lists upcoming visits within the
configured window (@pxref{Variable reference}).  In the visits roster,
@kbd{L} (or @kbd{C-c M l}) composes a @dfn{letter} from the record
under point: a narrative document describing the visit, which you edit
and file as you would any other document.  Letters are spell-checked
with @code{flyspell} when a @command{hunspell} or @command{aspell}
binary exists (@code{niori-letter-flyspell}), and optional
@code{yasnippet} templates ship in @file{snippets/}
(@pxref{Optional integrations}).

@node Lab tests
@section Lab tests

@cindex lab tests
The lab tests module tracks date, name, result, unit, reference range
and flag.  The dashboard shows the latest result of each test, with
abnormal flags, so an out-of-range result surfaces even when it was
recorded weeks ago.  Open the roster with @kbd{C-c M t}.

@node Vaccinations
@section Vaccinations

@cindex vaccinations
The vaccinations module tracks date, vaccine, dose, route, lot,
provider and next due.  The dashboard lists boosters that are due or
overdue within the configured window.  Open the roster with
@kbd{C-c M c}.

@node Documents
@section Documents

@cindex documents
@cindex attachments
Any file---a PDF lab report, a DOCX letter, a photograph---can be
attached to a visit, lab test, medication or vaccination.  Attach it
with @kbd{A} in the record's detail view.  The file is copied into the
data directory, one folder per record, so copying or syncing the data
directory backs up the whole record (@pxref{The data directory});
@code{niori-attachments-import-method} can also move or symlink instead
(@pxref{Variable reference}).

Attached documents open with @code{doc-view} (PDF), @code{image-mode}
(images) or an external viewer for formats Emacs cannot display, such
as DOCX or XLSX.

@kbd{C-c M f} opens the list of every document you have attached:

@table @kbd
@item RET
Open the document.
@item f
Open it with the external viewer.
@item o
Show its folder in Dired.
@item r
Retitle it.
@item d
Detach it; Niori asks before removing the file.
@end table

@noindent
The safety rules behind these buffers---relative paths, checksums and
orphan handling---are described in @ref{Attachment safety}.

@node Exporting data
@section Exporting data

@cindex exports
@findex niori-export-org
Three export formats cover the common needs, and the output lands in
@file{exports/} inside the data directory (@pxref{The data directory}):

@table @kbd
@item C-c M E o
Export as Org (@code{niori-export-org}).
@item C-c M E c
Export as CSV.
@item C-c M E j
Export as FHIR JSON (@pxref{FHIR interoperability}).
@end table

@noindent
The Org export can be encrypted with EasyPG: invoke it with a prefix
argument, @kbd{C-u C-c M E o} (@pxref{Encryption}).  CSV exports open
in @code{csv-mode} automatically when that package is installed.  If
you keep narrative notes in Org files of your own, @code{org-ql} can
run structured queries over exported Org archives
(@pxref{Optional integrations}).

@node History and revisions
@section History and revisions

@cindex history
@findex niori-record-ediff
Every update and delete first snapshots the current record, as JSON,
into the @code{revisions} table---an audit trail inside the same
database file (@pxref{Revisions and audit trail}).  Whether revisions
are kept at all is controlled by @code{niori-store-keep-revisions}
(@pxref{Variable reference}).

@kbd{D} on any record in a roster, or @kbd{C-c M D}, opens an
@code{ediff} between the pretty-printed current record and its previous
revision, so you can see exactly what changed.

@node Backups
@section Backups

@cindex backups
@findex niori-store-backup
@kbd{C-c M b} (@kbd{M-x niori-store-backup}) copies the database to a
timestamped file in @file{backups/} inside the data directory.  Keep a
copy on offline media; restoring one is described in @ref{Restoring a
database}.  Because the data directory also holds every attached
document, the directory itself is the unit of backup and relocation
(@pxref{Backups and relocation}).

@node FHIR interoperability
@section FHIR interoperability

@cindex FHIR
@findex niori-fhir-export
@kbd{C-c M E j} (@kbd{M-x niori-fhir-export}) writes a module as a FHIR
R4 collection Bundle:

@table @asis
@item Medications
become @code{MedicationStatement} resources;
@item Visits
become @code{Encounter} resources;
@item Lab tests
become @code{Observation} resources (numeric results as
@code{valueQuantity}, flags as @code{H}, @code{L} and @code{A}
interpretation codes);
@item Vaccinations
become @code{Immunization} resources.
@end table

@noindent
The mapping is intentionally minimal---display strings, no code-system
translation---which is right for personal export and review.

For retrieval, set @code{niori-fhir-server-url} to the server's base
URL and keep the bearer token in @code{auth-source}; then @kbd{M-x
niori-fhir-fetch} issues authenticated requests with the built-in
@code{url} library and returns parsed JSON (@pxref{Network access}).

